  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nBlocky pattern will remain in place across North America through the\nweekend with mid level ridge slowly expanding north northeast.\nSurface high over the upper Great Lakes will shift eastward. This\nwill keep low level winds with a dry easterly component. Will \ncontinue to see very few clouds, with long periods of clear sky. \nTemperature forecast is near persistence until Sunday when readings \nwill warm a bit. \n\nBlocking will break down early next week with a short wave moving\nacross the region Tuesday into Wednesday. This should lead to a cold\nfrontal passage, although at this stage the front looks like it will\nbe moisture starved.",
